# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Gospel News Access — files Git must NEVER upload.
#
# Plain English: anything listed here is invisible to Git. It stays on the
# machine it was written on and never reaches GitHub, never reaches the public
# website. This file is committed FIRST, before anything else exists, so there
# is no window in which a private file could be committed by accident.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- The private church and pastor roster. NEVER published. ---
# Direct contacts, administrator names, relationship notes, outreach history.
# NOTE the trailing /* — it matters. If you exclude the DIRECTORY ("private/")
# Git will not look inside it at all, and the "!" line below can never take
# effect. Excluding the CONTENTS lets us keep the README while everything else
# in the folder stays invisible to Git forever.
private/*
!private/README.md

# --- Credentials. There must never be a key, token or password in this repo. ---
# Every secret lives in GitHub Secrets (Settings > Secrets and variables >
# Actions). If any of these patterns ever matches a real file, something has
# gone wrong — stop and rotate the key.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials.json
client_secret*.json
service-account*.json
secrets.json
*.secret
token.txt
*_token
*_apikey
*.apikey

# --- Zoom / dial-in material. Never publishable. See cdc/ safety rules. ---
zoom-*.txt
*meeting-codes*
*dial-in*

# --- Python noise ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

# --- Editor / OS noise ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
